{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Node1 provides a persistent FTP destination for the scanner account from access.txt, confined to a dedicated dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The scanner account has `/srv/scanner-dropbox` as its home, a noninteractive shell, private directory/file permissions, and an allowlisted, enabled vsftpd service. After node1 restarted with a new boot identity, the service, listener, account data, hashes, permissions, firewall rules, and SELinux enforcement were recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2daf0d0ffb694f04","cmd-ef5570c0f972454a","cmd-c938896df7c84afd","cmd-75b3bada7be8423b","cmd-1e949c32812748e5","cmd-55d090c78d234a1f","cmd-eca2581a038d4c76","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Node2 can use passive FTP to upload and retrieve scanner files, including the supplied sample scan.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 forced classic PASV mode, listed the dropbox, retrieved the staged handover file, uploaded and retrieved sample-scan.txt, and verified matching hashes. Upload, retrieval, listing, and content verification also succeeded after both nodes had restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bb4e145300b64b8b","cmd-b68cf214dad8439f","cmd-95eb4d2c4eae4c90","cmd-4bef9bc5de0845dd"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"The scanner account cannot access host files outside its dedicated dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A direct traversal attempt for `/etc/passwd` was denied. The server configuration and filesystem observations support chroot confinement, and the denial was repeated successfully after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-08c8e649389b46a5","cmd-ef5570c0f972454a","cmd-0d173b9fa15f45a4"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Anonymous FTP access is unavailable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous authentication was directly rejected before and after the restart sequence, while configuration showed anonymous access disabled.","evidence_ids":["cmd-08c8e649389b46a5","cmd-ef5570c0f972454a","cmd-0d173b9fa15f45a4"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8. Node1 used the RHEL 9 vsftpd package, and lifecycle package-health checks remained successful.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5e4e4475ca0449e7","cmd-6a55fd3302f24aec","cmd-1ad619d5ec224b6f","cmd-eca2581a038d4c76","cmd-4bef9bc5de0845dd","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary state-changing mutations were identified. Package installation, account/dropbox creation, FTP configuration, SELinux and firewall changes, service enablement, sample transfers, and both restarts each had a clear task or mandatory evidence role. Temporary client directories were guarded by cleanup traps. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, no package-health damage, and only the intended FTP listener on node1. Both restart protocols are complete and independently corroborated by changed lifecycle boot identities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ad619d5ec224b6f","cmd-2daf0d0ffb694f04","cmd-63c5d0a605144e40","cmd-bb4e145300b64b8b","cmd-75b3bada7be8423b","cmd-007d37b2e554479b","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Passive upload and retrieval, sample integrity, confinement, and anonymous denial were demonstrated from node2. The configuration and data survived node1 and node2 restarts, whose changed boot identities are independently corroborated by lifecycle observations.","limitations":[] }
